@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: how proveo reads an on/off environment switch — one vocabulary, one parser, and the scan that keeps it that way
' covers: internal/envflag/**
' covers: internal/contract/env_switch_vocabulary_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/provision_test.go
'   the variables themselves .......... _spec/internal/envreg/env-registry.puml
'   PROVEO_DOCKER_PUSH / _PULL ......... _spec/_devops/buildx-driver-selection.puml
'   the decision record ............... _spec/_plans/repo-simplification.puml (N6)
'   shell switches outside envflag .... _spec/_plans/repo-simplification.puml (N32)
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT IT REPLACED (N6, DONE (wt) 2026-10-18) ────────────────────────────
' Before N6 each switch parsed its own value. The first read counted about
' twenty-two hand-rolled parsers in six vocabularies; the scan below flagged 24
' sites when it first ran (reported). PROVEO_WIZARD was parsed twice. A word
' could mean "on" at one site and nothing at the next: PROVEO_CDN_REQUIRE_DIST
' accepted only "1", and SKIP_GIT_HOOKS ignored "TRUE".
'
' ── THE VOCABULARY (MEASURED, internal/envflag/envflag.go) ─────────────────
'   On(v)         1 · true · yes · on · enable · enabled
'   Off(v)        0 · false · no · off · disable · disabled
'   Bool(v, def)  On → true · Off → false · anything else → def
' Matching ignores case and surrounding spaces.
' Reported: the set is the union of every spelling a converted site accepted,
' so no site lost one. An unknown value keeps the site's old behaviour — its
' default almost everywhere — and no default changed.
'
' ── WHICH QUESTION A SITE ASKS ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' A default-on switch asks Off(v), or Bool(v, true), which is the same test. A
' default-off switch asks On(v). Either way an unrecognised value leaves the
' switch at its default. MEASURED call sites (default in brackets):
'   PROVEO_CLONE [on], PROVEO_MOUNT_ROOT_DEPS [on] ...... internal/run/helpers.go
'   PROVEO_STDIN_FILTER [on], PROVEO_WIZARD [on] ........ internal/agentio/agentio.go
'   PROVEO_SBX_AGENT_KIT [on] ........................... internal/sbx/agents.go
'   PROVEO_SBX_RELOAD [off] ............................. internal/sbx/template.go
'   PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL_PULL [on], _FORCE [off] .......... internal/sbx/host_ollama.go
'   PROVEO_MOUNT_GH_CONFIG [on] ......................... internal/credentials/credentials.go
'   PROVEO_BUILDKIT_CACHE [on], PROVEO_DOCKER_PUSH [off]  internal/imagebuild/imagebuild.go
'   PROVEO_KEEP_AGENT_LOGINS [off] ...................... internal/proveohome/proveohome.go
'   PROVEO_SBX_MCP [off] ................................ internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go
'   PROVEO_UNINSTALL_ASSUME_YES [off] ................... cmd/proveo/uninstall.go
'   SKIP_GIT_HOOKS [off] ................................ cmd/proveo-dev/hooks.go
'   PROVEO_CDN_REQUIRE_DIST [off] ....................... cmd/proveo-dev/stagecdn.go
'
' PROVEO_WIZARD has ONE reader with ONE name, agentio.WizardEnabled(). MEASURED:
' run.WizardEnabled is deleted; internal/run (run.go twice, choices.go
' cacheApplies), internal/backend/sandbox/confirm.go and cmd/proveo/provision.go
' call agentio.WizardEnabled directly, as does cmd/proveo/wizard_test.go.
' MEASURED: internal/run imports internal/backend/sandbox (run.go
' sandbox.PlanPorts), so a reader in internal/run would close an import cycle
' for the sandbox package; agentio is a leaf both can import.
'
' ── ENUMS: THEIR OWN WORDS FIRST, THEN envflag ─────────────────────────────
' MEASURED:
'   PROVEO_GLYPHS          ascii → ASCII; none or any OFF word → no glyphs;
'                          anything else → Nerd (internal/ui/ui.go GlyphTierFrom)
'   PROVEO_DOCKER_PULL     "" or auto → no --pull; never or OFF → --pull=false;
'                          always or ON → --pull=true; anything else fails.
'                          The value is lowercased and trimmed before ANY
'                          match, so " Never " and "ALWAYS" work as the envflag
'                          words do; the error quotes the raw value
'                          (internal/imagebuild/imagebuild.go PullFlags;
'                          TestPullFlagsFromEnv adds " Never ", "ALWAYS", "Auto")
'   PROVEO_AUTO_PROVISION  ON builds; OFF declines; anything else asks, and only
'                          on a TTY with the wizard on (cmd/proveo/provision.go
'                          provisionConfirm). TestProvisionConfirmFollowsAuto-
'                          ProvisionBeforeTheWizard (cmd/proveo/provision_test.go),
'                          with PROVEO_WIZARD=0: yes, 1 or Enabled build;
'                          disabled, 0, "" or maybe decline. So AUTO_PROVISION
'                          is read before the wizard and wins over it.
'
' ── e2e OPT-IN GATES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' MEASURED: PROVEO_TOOLCHAIN_TEST (7 sites, e2e/toolchain_test.go),
' PROVEO_IDLE_TEST (1, idle_test.go) and PROVEO_LADDER_TEST (2, ladder_test.go)
' read through envflag.On instead of `!= "1"`.
' The scan does not walk e2e/, so nothing keeps a new e2e gate on envflag.
'
' ── OUT OF SCOPE BY DESIGN ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A typed prompt answer is not an env switch: wizard.go's y/yes and the
' uninstall prompt keep their own words. A presence check (`!= ""`) asks whether
' a value exists, not what it says. The scan walks Go only; image entrypoints
' parse their switches in shell, with their own spellings — e.g. PROVEO_SMOKE_TEST
' turns on only for "1" (packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh:176). Filed as N32.
'
' ── THE GUARD (internal/contract/env_switch_vocabulary_test.go) ────────────
' TestEnvSwitchesParseThroughEnvflag parses every non-test Go file under cmd/
' and internal/, skipping internal/envflag and testdata. Inside each function
' it taints what a call whose name ends in "env" returns (os.Getenv,
' os.LookupEnv, b.env) and what a func(string) string parameter returns, then
' follows assignments. It fails a tainted value compared with, or switched on,
' an on/off word. It also fails any `case` that lists two or more on/off words,
' tainted or not — the shape a hand-rolled helper takes. Reported: before the
' conversion it flagged exactly the 24 known sites and no prompt answer.
' TestEnvSwitchScanFlagsHandRolledParsers pins the scan itself: 6 snippets it
' must flag, 6 it must pass. internal/envflag/envflag_test.go
' TestOnOffBoolVocabulary covers every spelling, case, spaces and an unknown
' value falling back to the default.
' KNOWN LIMIT (review, recorded, not fixed): taint flows only through plain
' identifiers. A value stored in a struct field, a map or a slice, then compared
' with an on/off word, escapes the scan.
title envflag — one on/off vocabulary for every environment switch

component "os.Getenv · getenv(name)\nthe raw value" as RAW <<app>>

node "internal/envflag" as EF <<host>> {
  component "On(v)\n1 true yes on enable enabled" as ON <<app>>
  component "Off(v)\n0 false no off disable disabled" as OFF <<app>>
  component "Bool(v, def)\nOn → true · Off → false · else def" as BOOL <<app>>
}

node "Sites" as SITES <<host>> {
  component "default-on\nOff(v) or Bool(v, true)" as DON <<app>>
  component "default-off\nOn(v)" as DOFF <<app>>
  component "enums: GLYPHS · DOCKER_PULL\nAUTO_PROVISION" as ENUM <<app>>
}

component "TestEnvSwitchesParseThroughEnvflag\nAST scan of cmd/ and internal/" as SCAN <<app>>
component "a hand-rolled parser\nv == ""1"" · case ""off"", ""0""" as HAND <<error>>
component "prompt answers · presence checks\nnot switches" as NOT <<app>>

RAW ARROW_MAIN SITES
DON ARROW_MAIN OFF
DON ARROW_MAIN BOOL
DOFF ARROW_MAIN ON
ENUM ARROW_OPTIONAL EF : on/off words only
BOOL ARROW_MAIN ON
BOOL ARROW_MAIN OFF
SCAN ARROW_ERROR HAND : fails the test
SCAN ARROW_OPTIONAL NOT : passes by design

note bottom of EF
  **One word list, the union of the old ones.**
  Every spelling a converted site already
  accepted is still accepted, so merging the
  parsers changed no existing operator
  configuration.
end note

note right of SITES
  **The default decides which question to ask.**
  A default-on switch tests Off and a default-off
  switch tests On, so an unrecognised value,
  typically a typo, preserves the documented
  default instead of inverting it.
end note

note bottom of ENUM
  **Enumerations check their own words first.**
  Specific values such as ascii, never and
  always are matched before envflag, so only the
  generic on/off spellings reach the shared
  vocabulary.
end note

note bottom of SCAN
  **The scan follows the value, not the name.**
  It taints what a call ending in env returns,
  follows assignments, and fails a tainted
  comparison with an on/off word, so renaming a
  local variable cannot hide a parser.
end note

note bottom of NOT
  **Prompt answers are not environment switches.**
  Interactive confirmations and presence checks
  deliberately keep their own logic, and the
  scanner's self-test requires three such
  snippets to remain unflagged.
end note
@enduml
